althy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1 was the version the service was running with a 0.18 error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and next steps. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't confirmed yet that the error rate has returned to baseline. Someone should check that, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anything is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019wsHkqELEVSYTwpDGrmjhk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BpkWxzjJ6pkrCm4mgTmibV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0. Production is currently on v2.3.1, which is unhealthy, so I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ND5bptiMZmsEGHMndTfixA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XLG4QecuxoBjDqGPY2Qwk1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production release (error rate ~18%). Release history shows v2.3.1 unhealthy in production; v2.3.0 was the most recent release healthy in production. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reports VERIFIED and all three regions now run v2.3.0. Next steps: confirm error rate returns to baseline, investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release, and check the status of v2.3.1-rc (unhealthy in staging).", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports verified, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1 was the version the service was running with a 0.18 error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and next steps. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't confirmed yet that the error rate has returned to baseline. Someone should check that, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anything is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}